    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. **Missing named exports in finetune/index.js**\n   - **Problem**: The test file was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only in the default export\n   - **Solution**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` while keeping the default export for backward compatibility\n\n### 2. **Incorrect toxicity metric scoring in eval/metrics.js**\n   - **Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function was receiving `references` as the second parameter from `runEvaluations`, but it expected `bannedTerms`. This caused reference text to be used as banned terms instead of checking for actual toxic keywords, resulting in wrong scores\n   - **Solution**: Updated the function signature to accept `references` as the second parameter (for consistency with other metrics), so it correctly uses the default banned terms\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 **All 28 tests passing** across frai-core:\n- 8 test files: all passing\n- Specific tests fixed:\n  - `src/finetune/governance.test.js` - \"flags schema violations with descriptive errors\"\n  - `src/eval/index.test.js` - \"runs default evaluations\"\n\nPublic exports remain unchanged and fully backward compatible.",
